        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/CT-3300> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "1. Electrical Specifications Parameter Value Unit Notes Nominal current range 0 to 20 A rms Accuracy class Class 0.5 — IEC 61869-2 Continuous overload rating 14 A See note 2 Short-time overload 20 A < 1 second Output signal 4–20 mA Operating temperature -25 to +70 °C Note 2 — Continuous Overload Rating: The sensor is rated for continuous operation up to 14 A. Operation between 14 A and 20 A is permissible for short durations (< 60 seconds). Sustained operation above 14 A will cause progressive accuracy drift. ElectroMeasure recommends that process alarm thresholds triggering corrective action be set no higher than the continuous overload rating." .

    <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/chunk/DS-MECH-4400-s1> a ns1:Chunk ;
        rdfs:label "DS-MECH-4400 §1. Pressure Transmitter PRS-4410" ;
        ns1:mentions <https://rai-hackathon.bbger.at/kg/sensormodel/PRS-4410> ;
        ns1:page 1 ;
        ns1:text "1. Pressure Transmitter PRS-4410 Parameter Value Unit Measuring range 0 to 10 bar Accuracy (total error) ±0.10 bar (±0.075% FS) Repeatability ±0.025 bar Long-term stability ±0.05/year bar Media temperature -10 to +80 °C Application Note — Alarm Threshold Setting: With a total accuracy of ±0.10 bar, alarm thresholds should be set at least 5× the accuracy (0.50 bar) from the nominal operating point to avoid nuisance alarms. Thresholds closer than 3× accuracy (0.30 bar) are not recommended for process control." .

